  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/... \nIssued at 250 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nA cold front will progress southward on Monday night, with some\nuncertainty how quickly it moves through the area. Because of\nthat and the very humid and hot conditions during the daytime\nMonday, have the headlines going all the way through 10 PM. The\nfrontal convergence may be enough to overcome any weaknesses in\nthe cap, which again could be northwest Illinois but still an \noverall low signal for convection in our CWA.\n\nOne note for behind the front is the potential for smoke in the\nair, possibly even reduced air quality at the surface. GOES \nGeocolor satellite this afternoon indicated widespread smoke \nover the northern CONUS Rockies into the western Dakotas. RAP \nand HRRR extended smoke forecasts indicate this being steered \nsouthward behind the front over our area. This is still too far\nout to tell if it would mix to near-surface, but at least some \nsmoky sky Monday night into early Tuesday looks probable.\n\nAfter quiet and near to slightly warmer than seasonable\ntemperatures Wednesday and into the day Thursday, a slow moving\nand fairly well-defined short wave is indicated by guidance to \npass over the area late Thursday night into Friday. This looks \nlike the next chance of rain.",
